{"id":"e5ab6c65-bf33-4565-9cfc-2e2f6b28ea6d","object":"chat.completion","created":1784812483,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    payload = case['payload']\\n    items = payload['items']\\n    required = set(payload['required_failure_items'])\\n    current = list(items)\\n    n = 2\\n    attempts = 0\\n    while n <= len(current):\\n        base = len(current) // n\\n        rem = len(current) % n\\n        starts = []\\n        ends = []\\n        pos = 0\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            size = base + (1 if i < rem else 0)\\n            starts.append(pos)\\n            ends.append(pos + size)\\n            pos += size\\n        removed = False\\n        for i in range(n):\\n            start = starts[i]\\n            end = ends[i]\\n            candidate = current[:start] + current[end:]\\n            attempts += 1\\n            if required.issubset(candidate):\\n                current = candidate\\n                n = max(2, n - 1)\\n                removed = True\\n                break\\n        if not removed:\\n            n = min(len(current), 2 * n)\\n    one_minimal = True\\n    for i in range(len(current)):\\n        candidate = current[:i] + current[i+1:]\\n        if required.issubset(candidate):\\n            one_minimal = False\\n            break\\n    return {\\n        'reduced_items': current,\\n        'attempts': attempts,\\n        'one_minimal': one_minimal\\n    }\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a JSON object with key \"implementation\" containing Python source code defining `solve(case)`. The task: implement chunk reduction schedule. The description: \"Apply deterministic chunk-removal and granularity-refinement passes while preserving a supplied syntax and interestingness oracle.\" We are given a case with items (list of strings), required_failure_items (list of strings). The goal seems to be to reduce the list of 